<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Nightingale returns for her ME/CFS review eleven weeks after the diagnosis. She has had three sessions with the occupational therapist and now works in 30- to 45-minute blocks with lying-down rests between them, stopping before she feels spent. Her diary shows two crashes in the past two months, each after a day she broke the plan to meet a deadline, compared with one or two a week before. She drinks about 2.2 L a day, salts her meals, and wears compression garments; she is lightheaded on standing two or three times a week rather than daily. She still wakes unrefreshed but less heavy. Muscle aches are milder and she takes acetaminophen about once a week. She takes cholecalciferol every day. She wants to add an hour of work a day. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Interval change</td><td>Two crashes in two months, down from one or two a week</td></tr><tr><td>Energy management</td><td>Work in 30- to 45-minute blocks with rests; three occupational therapist sessions</td></tr><tr><td>Orthostatic symptoms</td><td>Two or three times a week, down from daily</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>Still unrefreshing but improved</td></tr><tr><td>Pain</td><td>Milder; acetaminophen about once a week</td></tr><tr><td>Patient goal</td><td>Add an hour of work a day</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
